  "chapterId": "chapter-0006",
  "segment": 1,
  "thesis": "Boundaries belong to knowledge; competence maps show conditions and failure surfaces obscured by global expert labels. Outfinitism begins with finite situated agents and open-ended revision, neither rejecting mathematical infinity nor promising final total explanation. Formal, computability, resource, predictability, statistical, representational, institutional and normative limits require different assumptions and remedies. Limit maps record task, context, resources, validated region, failure variables and signatures, self-detection, recovery and externalities; boundary discovery itself can be benchmarked. Explanation distance is a domain-specific profile of predictive, interventional, counterfactual, scope, compression, normative, provenance and confidence gaps, not a universal metric. Research should test boundary discovery, causal faithfulness, debt, distinction quality, model switching, communication, institutional correction and conditional limit patterns; wisdom benchmarks remain speculative. Limit sensitivity becomes architectural humility through evidence access, prediction records, protected dissent, rollback and calibration. Limit claims need specific levels, tests and dates; some boundaries move while others constitute or protect systems, and the boundary observer is limited too.",
  "role": "All chapters 22–29 analyzed individually.",
